ZREADER 0.8.0 — LOCAL BUILD / TEST REPORT

ARM static arm-linux-musleabihf / cortex_a53; MuPDF 1.28.6. Runtime pause list unchanged:
awesome volumd blanket Xorg. Own process core dumps disabled in launcher and C time64 helper setup.
Hardware inversion/night-mode settings untouched.

FLICKER
The old imageHeavy rule treated grey photographed paper as heavy ink: scan-D's
image coverage is ~0.8, background adds ~0.3-0.4 average ink even on ordinary text.
Baseline all 372/372 pages chose GC16 FULL. A separate periodic default cleaned
ordinary books every eight turns. Neither requires a double/progressive draw:
the actual pump already submitted once per rendered page.
New paper-relative broad tonal occupancy distinguishes text scans from real photos.
All 372-page audit: 353 REAGL, 19 GC16 (opening, cover departure, photo insert
pages 179-194 and photo departures). Page 179 was visually checked: real photos.
Actual UI script: opening plus 15 turns = 16 submissions before AND after.
Before: 16 GC16. After: 2 GC16 for opening/cover departure, then exactly 14 REAGL.
REAGL uses the driver's FULL update flag but is not a flashing GC16 cleanup.
No independent battery update; its pixels are composed into the same raster.
Existing periodic settings migrate OFF once (refresh_policy 8); future explicit
menu choices persist. No cleanup label is drawn on the reading canvas.
digital-big actual UI pages 1/2/3/4 remain GC16/GC16/REAGL/REAGL; cover-overlay
close still cleans. Image-only clipped dithering and text-AA pixel tests pass.

COVERS
v0.7 already contained a disk cache, but serial whole-EPUB pagination on a miss
blocked queued disk hits behind it. v0.8 has separate disk-read/generation workers,
page-one/first-spine-only extraction, immediate title/type placeholders, progressive
fill and next-page prefetch. Cache key: path+size+nanosecond mtime+format version.
32 RAM thumbnails (~384 KiB). 96x128 8-bit disk thumbnails, 12,288 bytes each.
Persistent cover cache <=10 MiB, plus one <=12 KiB temporary raster.
Seven large EPUB cold covers: 6415 ms before, 117 ms after (box, sequential).
Seven cached covers ready in 21 ms with renderer explicitly forbidden.
A cached hit stays 20 ms even while another child deliberately takes two seconds.
Changed file size/mtime invalidates identity; cap eviction and symlink preservation pass.

OPENING
Full EPUB pagination formerly happened before display, with redundant original/styled
layouts in the main document and two workers. Current-chapter anchor indexing was
also on the initial path even with no saved anchor/notes. PDF file open itself is
sub-millisecond here; image decode/rasterization dominates scan-D (~226 ms).
v0.8 reuses the main document for the first raster, defers full cold EPUB pagination,
streams available chapter counts, renders early requested pages while counting,
uses one EPUB worker, cancels abandoned pagination at chapter boundaries and
cancels stale raster work. Persistent typography-keyed MuPDF accelerators: at most
128 files of <=16 KiB (~2 MiB). No upfront anchor extraction without a saved anchor
or legacy annotation migration. 80-chapter synthetic fixture is 4,400 pages in the
probe layout, 5,040 at the app's styled layout. Eight early turns pass while counting.

Box first submit from process launch (warm OS filesystem cache, fresh application data):
                       v0.7        v0.8 cold       v0.8 warm
scan-D              252 ms      230 ms          255 ms
digital-big             124 ms       90 ms           90 ms
digital-small                  53 ms       47 ms           45 ms
Large synthetic EPUB   >7738 ms      20 ms           43 ms
Baseline EPUB had NO frame within its 6-second post-open observation window;
>7738 ms is a lower bound, not a measured eventual completion time.
The existing device digital-small render p50 is 21,870 us (53 jobs), versus 3,640 us
in the host baseline sample (5 jobs): approximately 6x CPU factor, different page
samples, NOT a controlled device benchmark. Using 6x plus ~250 ms panel time gives
rough v0.8 estimates: scan-D 1.6-1.8 s, digital-big 0.8 s, digital-small 0.5 s,
synthetic EPUB 0.4-0.5 s, cached library ~0.4 s plus text-composition overhead.
Use broad 3-8x uncertainty; on-device under-2-second opening is not verified.
Actual 10-20-second PDF opening stalls were NOT reproduced on this box.

STORAGE / BATTERY / STATE
Library uses statvfs(/mnt/us), shows free/total and all scanned book-file bytes,
plus per-row PDF/EPUB, size and relative folder. Books and documents are scanned.
Read-only powerd battLevel runs in the existing command worker at most every
three minutes. Bar/percentage appear top-right in library and reader; --% when
unknown. Mock asserts zero firmware writes and 76% readback. No sysfs writes.
The old direct Zig extern time() linked the legacy ARM time32 symbol with an
incorrect 64-bit return expectation. C wrapper emits a branch to __time64 in ARM
assembly; all new stamps are int64. Legacy opened=-2500945052 repairs to
1794022244. Positive old values remain readable. State JSON timestamp test passes.

